1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,184
Your head is older than
your feet.

2
00:00:02,434 --> 00:00:04,251
Every second you're
standing,

3
00:00:04,251 --> 00:00:06,381
it pulls a tiny bit
further ahead.

4
00:00:06,631 --> 00:00:07,675
Here's the rule.

5
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:09,828
Gravity doesn't just
pull on you.

6
00:00:09,828 --> 00:00:11,068
It slows down time.

7
00:00:11,318 --> 00:00:12,992
The closer you are to
Earth,

8
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:14,667
the slower your clock
ticks.

9
00:00:14,917 --> 00:00:16,228
Your feet are closer.

10
00:00:16,228 --> 00:00:17,477
Your head is higher.

11
00:00:17,477 --> 00:00:20,037
So your head's time runs
a little faster.

12
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:21,633
Sounds made up.

13
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:22,620
So in 2010,

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:26,837
physicists at a U.S. lab
called NIST tested it.

15
00:00:27,087 --> 00:00:27,973
They took two

16
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:29,882
super-precise atomic
clocks,

17
00:00:29,882 --> 00:00:31,996
and raised one by about
a foot.

18
00:00:31,996 --> 00:00:33,700
Two steps up a
staircase.

19
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,934
The higher clock ticked
faster.

20
00:00:36,184 --> 00:00:38,528
Over a whole
seventy-nine year life,

21
00:00:38,528 --> 00:00:40,546
those two steps add up
to about

22
00:00:40,546 --> 00:00:42,499
ninety billionths of a
second.

23
00:00:42,749 --> 00:00:44,459
Far too small to feel.

24
00:00:44,459 --> 00:00:45,159
But real.

25
00:00:45,409 --> 00:00:47,233
And your phone feels it.

26
00:00:47,233 --> 00:00:49,056
GPS satellites fly high,

27
00:00:49,056 --> 00:00:50,956
so their clocks run
fast.

28
00:00:51,206 --> 00:00:53,986
So engineers set them
slower on the ground,

29
00:00:53,986 --> 00:00:54,891
before launch.

30
00:00:54,891 --> 00:00:57,606
Without that fix, your
map would be wrong.

31
00:00:57,856 --> 00:00:58,930
Rule number one.

32
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:02,016
The higher you are, the
faster your time runs.

33
00:01:03,066 --> 00:01:05,228
So next time you take
the stairs,

34
00:01:05,228 --> 00:01:07,194
you just aged a little
faster.

35
00:01:07,194 --> 00:01:07,653
Barely.

36
00:01:07,903 --> 00:01:09,666
Which means your head
really

37
00:01:09,666 --> 00:01:11,177
is older than your feet.

38
00:01:11,177 --> 00:01:11,807
By a hair.

